          "title": "You'll want to know: ಸೈನ್ಯ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೈನ್ಯ — sainya — \"an army\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ರಾಜನ ಸೈನ್ಯ ನದಿಯನ್ನು ದಾಟಿತು. rājana sainya nadiyannu dāṭitu. The king's army crossed the river."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A soldier is a ಸೈನಿಕ; the army is the ಸೈನ್ಯ (sainya)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೈನ್ಯ (sainya) is borrowed from Sanskrit sainya, \"belonging to an army\", and as a noun \"an army\" (CDIAL 13602), from senā, \"an army\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
