          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೇನಾಪತಿ — sēnāpati — \"a commander; a general\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೇನಾಪತಿ ಸೈನಿಕರಿಗೆ ಮುಂದೆ ಹೋಗಲು ಹೇಳಿದನು. sēnāpati sainikarige munde hōgalu hēḷidanu. The general told the soldiers to go forward."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಸೇನಾಪತಿಗಳು, sēnāpatigaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೇನೆ, an army, and ಪತಿ, a lord."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಸೇನಾಪತಿ (sēnāpati) is borrowed from Sanskrit senāpati, \"the general of an army\" (Monier-Williams), from senā \"an army\" and pati \"a lord, a master\"."
            }
          ]
