          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯೋಧ (yōdha) is borrowed from Sanskrit yodha, \"a fighter, a warrior, a soldier\" (Monier-Williams), from the root yudh, \"to fight\", as in ಯುದ್ಧ."
